---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const releaseUrl = 'https://github.com/archievalmariano/crosspoint-reader/releases/tag/v1.0.3';
const sourceUrl = 'https://github.com/archievalmariano/crosspoint-reader/tree/v1.0.3';
const fileName = 'firmware-x4pro-g.factory.bin';
const downloadUrl = `https://github.com/archievalmariano/crosspoint-reader/releases/download/v1.0.3/${fileName}`;
const sha256 = '4654ad66d75cc64f91e4b76d2b5e10e40236c9dc976d7e84b4c533ca3633360f';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Install Project GOTO on the XTEINK X4 Pro — Archieval Mariano"
  description="A guide to installing Project GOTO (release v1.0.3) on the XTEINK X4 Pro over USB using esptool."
>
  <section class="wrap install">
    <p class="install__back"><a href="/desk/goto/">&larr; Project GOTO</a></p>

    <header class="install__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Project GOTO</p>
      <h1>Install Project GOTO on the XTEINK X4 Pro</h1>
    </header>

    <p class="install__lede">
      The current release is v1.0.3 (CrossPoint 1.6.0 + Apps 1.0.3). The X4 Pro
      installs over <strong>USB</strong> (direct flashing with <code>esptool</code>),
      not the microSD updater the original X4 uses. After that first install, later
      releases arrive over Wi-Fi.
    </p>
    <p class="install__note">
      Have the original XTEINK X4 instead? Use the
      <a href="/desk/goto/install/">microSD installation guide</a> — the download and steps
      are different.
    </p>

    <dl class="install__meta">
      <div><dt>Firmware</dt><dd><code>{fileName}</code> (factory image)</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Flash at</dt><dd><code>0x0</code></dd></div>
      <div><dt>SHA-256</dt><dd><code class="install__sha">{sha256}</code></dd></div>
      <div><dt>On-device identity</dt><dd><code>1.6.0-A1.0.3-G</code></dd></div>
    </dl>

    <p class="install__actions">
      <a class="install__download" href={downloadUrl}>Download {fileName}</a>
    </p>

    <p class="install__warn">This overwrites the device’s internal firmware and may reset internal flash state.</p>
    <p class="install__note">
      Saved <strong>Wi-Fi credentials</strong>, <strong>device/app settings</strong>,
      the <strong>NVS/configuration</strong> store, and <strong>OTA metadata /
      partition state</strong> can all be erased or reset. Do not expect internal
      settings to be preserved. This is separate from your <strong>microSD card</strong>,
      whose contents are not erased by flashing internal firmware.
    </p>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>Which file do I download?</h2>
      <p>
        Download <code>{fileName}</code>, the <strong>factory image</strong>. It is the
        normal installation file, and it is flashed at address <code>0x0</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want ON POINT, a P2P bus departure board, as well? Use
        <code>firmware-x4pro-gp.factory.bin</code> (GOTO + ON POINT) from the
        <a href={releaseUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">same release</a> instead,
        and check it against <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code> there. Everything below works
        the same way with that file name.
      </p>
      <p>
        The release also lists files without <code>.factory</code>, such as
        <code>firmware-x4pro-g.bin</code>. Those are app images used by the Wi-Fi
        updater. They are <strong>not</strong> installation files: <strong>never flash
        them at <code>0x0</code></strong>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <ul class="install__list">
        <li>Your XTEINK X4 Pro, charged.</li>
        <li>A USB-C cable that carries data (not charge-only).</li>
        <li>A computer (macOS, Linux, or Windows).</li>
        <li><strong>esptool</strong>, the standard Espressif flashing tool.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Verify the download before flashing (the value must match the SHA-256 above):</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>shasum -a 256 {fileName}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>1. Install esptool</h2>
      <p>With Python 3 installed:</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>pip install esptool</code></pre>
      <p>Then check it runs:</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>esptool version</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>2. Connect the X4 Pro and find its port</h2>
      <p>Plug the X4 Pro into the computer, then find the serial port:</p>
      <ul class="install__list">
        <li><strong>macOS:</strong> <code>ls /dev/cu.usbmodem*</code> → e.g. <code>/dev/cu.usbmodem101</code></li>
        <li><strong>Linux:</strong> <code>ls /dev/ttyACM* /dev/ttyUSB*</code> → e.g. <code>/dev/ttyACM0</code></li>
        <li><strong>Windows:</strong> Device Manager → Ports (COM &amp; LPT) → e.g. <code>COM5</code></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>3. Flash Project GOTO</h2>
      <p>Run the command for your platform, in the folder that holds the downloaded file. Point <code>--port</code> at what you found above.</p>
      <p class="install__subhead">macOS / Linux</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>esptool --chip esp32s3 --port /dev/cu.usbmodem101 --baud 921600 write_flash 0x0 {fileName}</code></pre>
      <p class="install__subhead">Windows</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>esptool --chip esp32s3 --port COM5 --baud 921600 write_flash 0x0 {fileName}</code></pre>
      <p>It takes about 40 seconds. Near the end you should see <code>Hash of data verified.</code> and the device reboots itself into CrossPoint.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>4. First boot</h2>
      <p>
        The X4 Pro restarts into CrossPoint. Open <strong>Apps</strong> on the home
        screen, then <strong>GOTO</strong> (it reads TOGO in the evening). In Settings,
        the version reads <code>1.6.0-A1.0.3-G</code>, or <code>1.6.0-A1.0.3-GP</code>
        with ON POINT.
      </p>
      <p>
        If Wi-Fi is not connected, GOTO opens CrossPoint’s Wi-Fi screen first. It
        tries your saved network; if that does not connect, choose your network from
        the list. Press Back to skip it and read the last saved edition.
      </p>
      <p class="install__subhead">Controls on the X4 Pro</p>
      <ul class="install__list">
        <li><strong>Left key</strong> → previous story · <strong>Right key</strong> → next story (wraps around)</li>
        <li><strong>Swipe left</strong> → next story · <strong>swipe right</strong> → previous story. This follows Settings → Controls → Touch Reader Controls, the same setting as books: Tap uses the screen’s sides instead, and Off turns touch page turns off.</li>
        <li>Tap the on-screen <strong>FULL STORY</strong> bar → show the article QR; tap the screen to go back</li>
        <li><strong>Back</strong> → return to Apps · <strong>Home</strong> → the CrossPoint home screen</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>Updating</h2>
      <p>
        Later releases install over Wi-Fi: connect to Wi-Fi, then open Settings &rarr;
        System &rarr; Check for updates. The update keeps the package you installed
        (GOTO, or GOTO + ON POINT). To switch packages, flash the other factory image
        over USB as above.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <ul class="install__list">
        <li><strong>esptool can’t connect.</strong> Hold the <strong>left navigation button</strong> while you plug in the USB cable (it doubles as the boot-select pin), keep holding for a second, then run the flash command again. Release once it starts writing.</li>
        <li><strong>Wrong or missing port.</strong> Try a different USB-C cable (many are charge-only), a different port, and re-check the port name while the device is plugged in.</li>
        <li><strong>Permission denied on Linux.</strong> Add yourself to the <code>dialout</code> group (<code>sudo usermod -aG dialout $USER</code>), then log out and back in.</li>
        <li><strong>It flashed but looks frozen.</strong> Give the first e-ink refresh a few seconds; if still stuck, re-run the flash command (it is safe to repeat).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="install__links">
      <a href={releaseUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Release notes</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source code</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/desk/goto/">Project GOTO</a>
    </p>

    <p class="install__note">
      Release v1.0.3 · XTEINK X4 Pro (ESP32-S3). The original XTEINK X4 installs the
      same release from microSD.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .install {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-xl);
  }
  .install__back {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .install__head {
    border-bottom: var(--heavy-rule);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .install__head h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }
  .install__lede {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
  }
  .install__meta {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
  }
  .install__meta div {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35em var(--space-sm);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .install__meta dt {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    min-width: 8rem;
  }
  .install__meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }
  .install__sha {
    word-break: break-all;
  }
  .install__actions {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
  }
  .install__download {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.15rem;
    border: var(--heavy-rule);
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .install__download:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  .install__section {
    margin-block: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .install__section h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .install__subhead {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .install__section p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .install__list {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .install__list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .install__note {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: var(--space-sm) 0 0;
  }
  .install__warn {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-xs);
  }
  .install__code {
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    overflow-x: auto;
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.82em;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .install__code code {
    font-size: inherit;
    white-space: pre;
  }
  .install__links {
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
  .install__links span {
    margin: 0 0.5em;
    color: var(--rule);
  }
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
</style>
